          ],
          "eyebrow": "Recap",
          "title": "What you've learned",
          "lede": "Every A/B test has the same three parts, and lift turns the raw rates into one interpretable figure.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stats_ab_test_lift.s08.b1",
              "role": "takeaway",
              "text": "Every A/B test has a **control group**, a **treatment group**, and the **measure** being compared between them. The treatment group's result is compared against the control \u2014 the baseline. Analysing the results means determining whether the variation had a **positive, negative, or neutral** effect. **Lift** puts the observed difference into one figure: a positive lift means the variation's rate came out above the control's in this test; a negative lift means it came out below.",
              "lineage": {
                "concept_ids": [
