            "stats.lift_interpretation"
          ],
          "eyebrow": "Let's review",
          "title": "Computing lift step by step",
          "lede": "The hands-on asked you to compute lift. Here's the calculation laid out clearly.",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "prose",
              "block_id": "tile_stats_ab_test_lift.r04.b1",
              "role": "definition",
              "text": "**Lift formula:** (treatment rate \u2212 control rate) \u00f7 control rate \u00d7 100. For the checkout test: (0.22 \u2212 0.20) \u00f7 0.20 \u00d7 100 = **10 % lift**. This is a relative improvement \u2014 it expresses the variation's change as a percentage of the baseline's rate, not as a raw percentage-point difference.",
