              "role": "example",
              "text": "Three cases to check your function against: (1) control=0.20, treatment=0.22 \u2192 **+10 % (positive)**. (2) control=0.25, treatment=0.20 \u2192 **\u221220 % (negative)**. (3) control=0.30, treatment=0.30 \u2192 **0 % (neutral)**. A positive lift means the variation's rate came out above the control's; a negative lift means it came out below.",
